well, at least, there is no (significant) evidence to the contrary under the assumption of linearity (in log-odds space). Also, this is under the assumption that the part you did not paste into the email (the fixed effect correlations) does not reveal large collinearity. Since it seems that you used treatment coding for the 3-way contrast, I assume, however, that you do have high collinearity. I would use Helmert coding, if you aren't already. This will also allow you to address your second question without recoding of the data.



 
