It seems to me that you got yourself a nice ceiling effect (pseudo is too high already, so it can't increase; keep in mind that the projection for the ideo group might only look like it goes even higher due to the assumption of linearity). if you plot the CIs, it will become apparent whether I am right. 

if you're familiar with ggplot2, I recommend you use the geom_smooth function for plotting (method = "glm", family="binomial") your data. It'll give you plots similar to the ones I attached.

