Dear Fotis,

I am finally back in town. When I read your email. I noticed that the chisq for the interaction was 3.8. Note that this still allows for one of the two interaction terms to be significant. You have not shown that this is not the case. More generally, I would not remove the interaction term from the model if this is a test you intended by design (the 3x2). For reasons not to do that, I suggest Harrell 2001's comments on model comparison and why it is anti-conservative. 

Florian



